One exterior edge at order34
============================

This is a working recovery of the fixed F012 lower clause n(4,6,12)>=35.
For a root edge its two depth-two Moore trees have26 vertices and exactly12 cross edges. The two leaf sides each have D=15 missing incidences. If the exterior has t vertices, quartic degree counting gives e(Y)=2t-15. Hence no order at most33 is possible; only n34 needs exclusion for the source bound.

At n34 there are eight exterior vertices and exactly one exterior edge yz. Its endpoints each have three old neighbours; the other six have four. No vertex can have two neighbours in the same one of the six rooted branches. The two endpoints together cannot repeat a branch either: this makes a triangle, quadrangle, or pentagon. Their six old neighbours therefore use all six branches. If u,v are their left degrees, u+v=3.

The six other left degrees a_i belong to{1,2,3} and sum to12. Their right degrees are4-a_i; endpoint right degrees are3-u,3-v. Thus the difference in side pair totals is sum(3a_i-6)+2(u+v)-6=0. The root-pair equations acquired from the accepted components give F_L=f(P_R),F_R=f(P_L), where f(P)=(45-sum d^2)/2. Only equal-profile roots can complete. The independently listed564 degree vectors give exactly the necessary pairs in outside_degrees01.json.

The accepted partial-matching forest normalization covers458 deficit-matrix orbits and12,864,538 matching products. The changed root visitor keeps exactly the necessary degree profiles; every canonical reuse still checks a literal adjacency-preserving bijection. The root pass alone is not a graph exclusion.

For b positive left-neighbour blocks,6<=b<=8, the three size counts are n3=F-15+b,n2=45-2F-3b,n1=3b+F-30. Append8-b empty blocks. Each empty block must be an endpoint; all endpoint block sizes sum to3. Install every possible unordered exterior edge, then attach all15 right incidences with endpoint capacity3-size and other capacity4-size. The same complete repeated-copy ordering and necessary distance/root-pair tests used in lambda14 preserve all completions. No remaining vertex or edge is left unspecified at completion.

These are analytic/coverage reductions only. Target root and boundary completions, fresh controls and distinct review are still required; no lower-bound clause is credited yet.
